cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, or any of the anatomical data in it, please cite it as
  below. The numbers carry their own primary sources on every card; please cite
  those as well where you rely on them. The code is under the MIT licence; the
  anatomical data, card text, documentation and rendered images are under
  CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-CONTENT).
title: Microalgae 3D Atlas
abstract: >-
  An interactive 3D cell atlas of microalgae and cyanobacteria, drawn from
  primary sources and stating the provenance of every measurement. The first
  specimen is Spirulina (Limnospira platensis), from the helical trichome under
  transmitted light down to a nanometre-scale cutaway of one cell. Each of its
  19 clickable structures carries dated dimensions marked at one of three
  confidence tiers — measured in Spirulina itself, taken from model
  cyanobacteria, or not yet established — so a reader can tell what is known
  from what is inferred. Chlorella vulgaris, Chlorella sorokiniana and Euglena
  gracilis follow as wet mounts, exterior only, seen through the same simulated
  light microscope. The constraints the numbers have to satisfy, and the shape
  every specimen record must have, are asserted in code rather than left as
  prose.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Russo
    given-names: Giovanni Luca
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4072-0331"
repository-code: https://github.com/giovannilucarusso-ui/Microalgae-3D-Atlas
url: https://giovannilucarusso-ui.github.io/Microalgae-3D-Atlas/
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
# One licence here, although the atlas has two and the format allows a list.
# Zenodo reads this file when it archives a release and rejects a list for this
# key with "Citation metadata load failed" (zenodo/zenodo#2515), so the release
# would never be archived. CC BY 4.0 is stated in `message` above and in
# LICENSE-CONTENT, and is added to the Zenodo record by hand.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - microalgae
  - cyanobacteria
  - Spirulina
  - Limnospira platensis
  - Arthrospira
  - Chlorella
  - Euglena gracilis
  - cell ultrastructure
  - interactive 3D
  - scientific visualisation
  - WebGL
# The concept DOI: it resolves to the newest archived release, so it stays right
# from one version to the next, and each release also has a DOI of its own on
# its Zenodo page. Zenodo does not read this key when it archives a release, so
# it cannot collide with the DOI the new release is given.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22738179
